        "file": "django/db/models/fields/json.py",
        "start_line": 432,
        "end_line": 436,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "medium",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Every Value is wrapped as JSON, even when its output_field is not a JSONField",
        "explanation": "The new condition JSON-wraps any expressions.Value on databases without a native JSON field. That is correct for Value(x, JSONField), whose compiled parameter is a JSON-encoded string. A Value the user supplied with a non-JSON output_field, such as Value(\"foo\") inferred as CharField, compiles to the raw 'foo'. The query then runs JSON_EXTRACT('foo', '$') on SQLite and MySQL, or JSON_OBJECT('value' VALUE 'foo' FORMAT JSON) on Oracle, and fails with a malformed-JSON error. Before this change such a Value skipped this block and was compared directly with the extracted left-hand value. Separately, Value(None) with no output_field compiles to ('NULL', []), so params[0] in the SQLite branch raises IndexError.",
        "suggestion": "Only treat the Value as JSON when its output_field is a JSONField, e.g. `not hasattr(param, \"as_sql\") or (isinstance(param, expressions.Value) and isinstance(param.output_field, JSONField))`, and add a test with a non-JSON Value in an __in list.",
        "evidence": "not hasattr(param, \"as_sql\") or isinstance(param, expressions.Value)",
        "confidence": 0.45,
